# Modular arithmetic: the arithmetic of remainders, where numbers wrap around a fixed modulus like hours on a clock.
# The remainder of n divided by k is always one of the k values from zero up to k minus one, and these bound facts are
# proved for EVERY n by the refinement prover (which models a remainder as an unknown pinned to its range) and checked
# by `seed test`. Modular arithmetic is how the twenty-four directions of the substrate compose: a direction plus a
# direction wraps within the twenty-four, the clock of the 24-cell.

# Every remainder modulo two is at least zero: n mod 2 >= 0, for every n.
task remainder-mod-two-non-negative
  take n, like integer
  like integer
  hold <a remainder modulo two is at least zero>
    call is-minimum
      call modulo
        read n
        code 2
      code 0
  send back
    read n

# Every remainder modulo two is below two: n mod 2 < 2, for every n. So a parity is always zero or one.
task remainder-mod-two-below-two
  take n, like integer
  like integer
  hold <a remainder modulo two is below two>
    call is-below
      call modulo
        read n
        code 2
      code 2
  send back
    read n

# Every remainder modulo three is at least zero: n mod 3 >= 0, for every n.
task remainder-mod-three-non-negative
  take n, like integer
  like integer
  hold <a remainder modulo three is at least zero>
    call is-minimum
      call modulo
        read n
        code 3
      code 0
  send back
    read n

# Every remainder modulo three is below three: n mod 3 < 3, for every n. The three residues are the ternary tone.
task remainder-mod-three-below-three
  take n, like integer
  like integer
  hold <a remainder modulo three is below three>
    call is-below
      call modulo
        read n
        code 3
      code 3
  send back
    read n

# Every remainder modulo twenty-four is below twenty-four: n mod 24 < 24, for every n. The directions of the 24-cell
# compose on this clock.
task remainder-mod-twenty-four-below-twenty-four
  take n, like integer
  like integer
  hold <a remainder modulo twenty-four is below twenty-four>
    call is-below
      call modulo
        read n
        code 24
      code 24
  send back
    read n
